f got < 0 { return .Err(sys.IoError::from_code(i32(-got))) }\n                mut raw := mode.saved.clone()\n                p := usize(addr(&mut raw[0]))\n                store_u32(ptr(p), load_u32(ptr(p)).bit_and(u32(0x5eb).bit_not()))\n                store_u32(ptr(p + 4), load_u32(ptr(p + 4)).bit_and(u32(1).bit_not()))\n                store_u32(ptr(p + 8), load_u32(ptr(p + 8)).bit_and(u32(0x130).bit_not()).bit_or(0x30))\n                store_u32(ptr(p + 12), load_u32(ptr(p + 12)).bit_and(u32(0x804b).bit_not()))\n                store_u8(ptr(p + 22), 0); store_u8(ptr(p + 23), 1)\n                set := sys.linux_syscall(29, mode.handle, 0x5402, i64(p), 0, 0, 0)\n                if set < 0 { return .Err(sys.IoError::from_code(i32(-set))) }\n            } else { return .Err(.Unsupported) }\n        }\n        mode.active = true\n        .Ok(move mode)\n    }\n\n    pub fn restore(&mut self) -> Result<(), sys.IoError> {\n        if !self.active { return .Ok }\n        unsafe {\n            if target_is(\"windows\") {\n                if set_mode(ptr(usize(self.handle)), u32(self.saved[0])) == 0 { return .Err(.BadDescriptor) }\n            } else if target_is(\"macos\") {\n                if tcsetattr(i32(self.handle), 0, addr(&self.saved[0])) != 0 { return .Err(sys.IoError::from_code(load_i32(errno_address()))) }\n            } else if target_is(\"linux\") {\n                status := sys.linux_syscall(29, self.handle, 0x5402, i64(usize(addr(&self.saved[0]))), 0, 0, 0)\n                if status < 0 { return .Err(sys.IoError::from_code(i32(-status))) }\n            }\n        }\n        self.active = false\n        .Ok\n    }\n\n    fn dispose(&mut self) {\n        if self.handle < 0 { return }\n        _ := self.restore()\n        unsafe {\n            if target_is(\"windows\") { _ := close_handle(ptr(usize(self.handle))) }\n            else if target_is(\"macos\") { _ := close_fd(i32(self.handle)) }\n            else if target_is(\"linux\") { _ := sys.linux_syscall(57, self.handle, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) }\n        }\n        self.handle = -1\n    }\n}\n" }
    if name == "text" { return "import std.text.grapheme as segmentation\nimport std.bytes as bytes\n\nfn matches_at(text: string, start: i32, needle: string) -> bool {\n    for i in 0..needle.len { if text[start + i] != needle[i] { return false } }\n    true\n}\npub fn starts_with(text: string, prefix: string) -> bool {\n    prefix.len <= text.len && matches_at(text, 0, prefix)\n}\npub fn ends_with(text: string, suffix: string) -> bool {\n    suffix.len <= text.len && matches_at(text, text.len - suffix.len, suffix)\n}\npub fn find(text: string, needle: string) -> Option<i32> {\n    if needle.len == 0 { return .Some(0) }\n    if needle.len > text.len { return .None }\n    for start in 0..(text.len - needle.len + 1) {\n        if matches_at(text, start, needle) { return .Some(start) }\n    }\n    .None\n}\npub fn contains(text: string, needle: string) -> bool {\n    find(text, needle).is_some()\n}\npub fn replace(text: string, from: string, to: string) -> string {\n    if from.len == 0 { return text.clone() }\n    first := match find(text, from) {\n        .Some(pos) => pos,\n        .None => { return text.clone() },\n    }\n    mut out: []u8 = []\n    out.reserve(text.len)\n    mut cursor := 0\n    mut pos := first\n    while pos <= text.len - from.len {\n        if matches_at(text, pos, from) {\n            for i in cursor..pos { out.push(u8(text[i])) }\n            bytes.append_utf8(&mut out, to)\n            cursor = pos + from.len\n            pos = cursor\n        } else { pos += 1 }\n    }\n    for i in cursor..text.len { out.push(u8(text[i])) }\n    bytes.decode(&out).unwrap()\n}\nfn ascii_case(text: string, to_upper: bool) -> string {\n    mut first := -1\n    for i in 0..text.len {\n        b := text[i]\n        if to_upper {\n            if b >= 97 && b <= 122 { first = i; break }\n        } else {\n            if b >= 65 && b <= 90 { first = i; break }\n        }\n    }\n    if first < 0 { return text.clone() }\n    mut out: []u8 = []\n    out.reserve(text.len)\n    for i in 0..first { out.push(u8(text[i])) }\n    for i in first..text.len {\n        mut b := text[i]\n        if to_upper {\n            if b >= 97 && b <= 122 { b -= 32 }\n        } else {\n            if b >= 65 && b <= 90 { b += 32 }\n        }\n        out.push(u8(b))\n    }\n    bytes.decode(&out).unwrap()\n}\npub fn lower(text: string) -> string { ascii_case(text, false) }\npub fn upper(text: string) -> string { ascii_case(text, true) }\nfn append_padding(out: &mut []u8, pattern: string, count: i32) {\n    mut remaining := count\n    while remaining > 0 {\n        for byte in pattern.bytes() {\n            if byte < 128 || byte >= 192 {\n                if remaining == 0 { return }\n                remaining -= 1\n            }\n            out.push(byte)\n        }\n    }\n}\nfn pad_text(text: string, width: i32, fill: string, left: bool) -> string {\n    count := text.runes().len\n    if count >= width { return text.clone() }\n    unit := if fill.len == 0 { \" \" } else { fill.clone() }\n    needed := width - count\n    mut out: []u8 = []\n    out.reserve(width)\n    if !left { bytes.append_utf8(&mut out, text) }\n    append_padding(&mut out, unit, needed)\n    if left { bytes.append_utf8(&mut out, text) }\n    bytes.decode(&out).unwrap()\n}\npub fn pad_left(text: string, width: i32, fill: string) -> string { pad_text(text, width, fill, true) }\npub fn pad_right(text: string, width: i32, fill: string) -> string { pad_text(text, width, fill, false) }\npub fn split(text: string, separator: string) -> []string {\n    mut parts: []string = []\n    if separator.len == 0 { parts.push(text.clone()); return parts }\n    mut start := 0\n    mut cursor := 0\n    while cursor <= text.len - separator.len {\n        if matches_at(text, cursor, separator) {\n            parts.push(text[start..cursor])\n            cursor += separator.len\n            start = cursor\n        } else { cursor += 1 }\n    }\n    if start == 0 { parts.push(text.clone()) }\n    else if start == text.len { parts.push(\"\") }\n    else { parts.push(text[start..text.len]) }\n    parts\n}\nfn whitespace(byte: i32) -> bool { byte == 32 || byte == 9 || byte == 10 || byte == 13 }\npub fn trim(text: string) -> string {\n    mut start := 0\n    mut end := text.len\n    while start < end && whitespace(i32(text[start])) { start += 1 }\n    while end > start && whitespace(i32(text[end - 1])) { end -= 1 }\n    if start == 0 && end == text.len { return text.clone() }\n    if start == end { return \"\" }\n    text[start..end]\n}\n@test fn text_search_and_split_handle_utf8_and_empty_parts() {\n    starts_with(\"åäö 🌍\", \"å\")\n    ends_with(\"åäö 🌍\", \"🌍\")\n    find(\"åäö 🌍\", \"🌍\") == .Some(7)\n    find(\"åäö 🌍\", \"missing\") == .None\n    parts := split(\"å::🌍::::\", \"::\")\n    parts.len == 4\n    parts[0] == \"å\"\n    parts[1] == \"🌍\"\n    parts[2] == \"\"\n    parts[3] == \"\"\n    trim(\" \\t å 🌍 \\r\\n\") == \"å 🌍\"\n    split(\"\", \"\").len == 1\n    contains(\"åäö 🌍\", \"äö\")\n    !contains(\"åäö\", \"xyz\")\n    replace(\"a::b::c\", \"::\", \"-\") == \"a-b-c\"\n    replace(\"åäö\", \"x\", \"y\") == \"åäö\"\n    replace(\"abc\", \"\", \"x\") == \"abc\"\n    replace(\"abab\", \"ab\", \"aba\") == \"abaaba\"\n    lower(\"Hello ÅÄÖ 🌍 123!\") == \"hello ÅÄÖ 🌍 123!\"\n    upper(\"Hello åäö 🌍 123!\") == \"HELLO åäö 🌍 123!\"\n    pad_left(\"42\", 5, \"0\") == \"00042\"\n    pad_left(\"åä\", 4, \"\") == \"  åä\"\n    pad_left(\"åäö\", 3, \" \") == \"åäö\"\n    pad_right(\"hi\", 5, \".\") == \"hi...\"\n    pad_right(\"🌍!\", 4, \"·\") == \"🌍!··\"\n    pad_right(\"hello\", 2, \" \") == \"hello\"\n}\n\n@test fn padding_repeats_and_truncates_fill_at_scalar_boundaries() {\n    assert(pad_left(\"x\", 4, \"å🌍\") == \"å🌍åx\")\n    assert(pad_right(\"x\", 4, \"🌍å\") == \"x🌍å🌍\")\n    assert(pad_right(\"\", 2, \"å🌍\") == \"å🌍\")\n    assert(pad_left(\"\", 1, \"🌍å\") == \"🌍\")\n}\n\npub opaque struct Graphemes { text: &str, offset: i32 }\npub opaque struct Grapheme { text: &str, start: i32, end: i32 }\n\npub fn graphemes(text: &str) -> Graphemes from text { Graphemes { text: text, offset: 0 } }\n\nimpl Grapheme {\n    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str from self { &self.text[self.start..self.end] }\n    pub fn start(&self) -> i32 { self.start }\n    pub fn end(&self) -> i32 { self.end }\n}\n\nimpl Iterator for Graphemes {\n    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<Grapheme> from self {\n        if self.offset == self.text.len { return .None }\n        start := self.offset\n        self.offset = segmentation.next_boundary(self.text, start)\n        .Some(Grapheme { text: self.text, start: start, end: self.offset })\n    }\n}\n" }
    if name == "text/grapheme" { return "import std.bytes.utf8\nimport std.text.grapheme_data as data\n\nconst CR: i32 = 1\nconst LF: i32 = 2\nconst CONTROL: i32 = 3\nconst EXTEND: i32 = 4\nconst ZWJ: i32 = 5\nconst RI: i32 = 6\nconst PREPEND: i32 = 7\nconst SPACING_MARK: i32 = 8\nconst L: i32 = 9\nconst V: i32 = 10\nconst T: i32 = 11\nconst LV: i32 = 12\nconst LVT: i32 = 13\n\nfn properties(cp: i32) -> i32 {\n    if cp >= 0xac00 && cp <= 0xd7a3 { return if (cp - 0xac00) % 28 == 0 { LV } else { LVT } }\n    ranges := data.RANGES\n    mut low := 0\n    mut high := ranges.len / 6\n    while low + 1 < high {\n        mid := (low + high) / 2\n        at := mid * 6\n        mut first := 0\n        for i in at..(at + 4) { first = first * 64 + i32(ranges[i]) - 35 }\n        if cp < first { high = mid } else { low = mid }\n    }\n    (i32(ranges[low * 6 + 4]) - 35) * 64 + i32(ranges[low * 6 + 5]) - 35\n}\n\nfn control(kind: i32) -> bool { kind >= CR && kind <= CONTROL }\n\nfn boundary(previous: i32, next: i32, indic_link: bool, emoji_join: bool, odd_regional: bool) -> bool {\n    kind := next.bit_and(15)\n    if previous == CR && kind == LF { return false }\n    if control(previous) || control(kind) { return true }\n    if previous == L && (kind == L || kind == V || kind == LV || kind == LVT) { return false }\n    if (previous == LV || previous == V) && (kind == V || kind == T) { return false }\n    if (previous == LVT || previous == T) && kind == T { return false }\n    if kind == EXTEND || kind == ZWJ || kind == SPACING_MARK || previous == PREPEND { return false }\n    if indic_link && next.bit_and(48) == 16 { return false }\n    if emoji_join && next.bit_and(64) != 0 { return false }\n    !(kind == RI && odd_regional)\n}\n\npub fn next_boundary(value: &str, start: i32) -> i32 {\n    bytes := value.as_bytes()\n    mut pos := start\n    mut previous := 0\n    mut indic := 0\n    mut emoji := false\n    mut emoji_join := false\n    mut odd_regional := false\n    while pos < value.len {\n        scalar := utf8.decode_prefix(&bytes[pos..])\n        match scalar {\n            .Scalar(cp, size) => {\n                next := properties(i32(cp))\n                if pos > start && boundary(previous, next, indic == 2, emoji_join, odd_regional) { break }\n                previous = next.bit_and(15)\n                incb := next.bit_and(48)\n                if incb == 16 { indic = 1 } else if incb == 48 && indic != 0 { indic = 2 } else if incb != 32 { indic = 0 }\n                emoji_join = previous == ZWJ && emoji\n                emoji = next.bit_and(64) != 0 || (previous == EXTEND && emoji)\n                odd_regional = previous == RI && !odd_regional\n                pos += size\n            },\n            _ => { assert(false) },\n        }\n    }\n    pos\n}\n" }
